# b6-innsbruck-stalemate: the battle of session 9 (Innsbruck, 1805), with the French army cut to
# 500 men, one unit (its VP field 5, which NAPOLEON.BAS multiplies by 100). The Allies defend and
# every unit of the player rests, each turn. The time runs out while neither side holds the field
# (possess = 0), so expire calls over(3), the end that no other battle reaches. PDS 7.1 wrote 3 as
# the winner there, which gives the battle to the defender; the port writes the same
# (docs\devnotes.md, step 8). The battle's BATTLE.$$$ is b6-innsbruck-stalemate.battle.
# seed 2 (NAP_SEED)

# A TICK of a second or more: any key ends it. A "hit a key" pause: a space. A unit's
# order: a space, which rests it.
rule 3 key f12
rule 1 key space
# The combat menu of a unit of the player that fights: Enter, the first item (Light Skirmish).
rule 2:C key enter
play until 5
# shot first-order
state
key space
rule 5 key space
# over writes OUTCOME.&&& and waits at place 7 before it exits (scriptend).
play until 7:O
# shot result
state
key f12
